for the browser - android.app.Activity/AlertDialog, android.widget.*
(TextView, Button, EditText, CheckBox, Switch, SeekBar, ImageView,
LinearLayout, FrameLayout, ScrollView, ListView, Spinner, ArrayAdapter,
Toast), android.view.* (View, ViewGroup, Gravity, Menu), android.os
(Bundle, Handler, Build), android.util.Log, android.graphics.Color,
SharedPreferences; Ruboto's RubotoActivity/ScriptInfo/RubotoDialog; the
lesson app's R (drawables); and org.chunkybacon.sim.Device, the phone they
run on (clock, logcat, toasts, dialogs, snapshot as JSON). They draw
nothing: the page draws the snapshot. The lifecycle is driven from Ruby
(chunkybacon's html/ruboto_sim/ruboto_sim.rb).

