From a38020b7e6b7c225654732b181a5c6100e3b2620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Largo <Largo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:52:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix ReferenceQueue typing (TeaVM), strict Bundle for the
 simulated phone

teavm-plugin: TeaVM 0.16.0's WeakReferenceDependencyListener makes a new
dependency node on every method it is called for, and connects the queue
argument of WeakReference.<init> instead of the reference, so to the
analysis ReferenceQueue.poll() returns nothing. Methods called only on
polled references were dropped from their classes: JRuby's
ObjectProxyCache.Segment.expunge calls EntryRef.hash() on them, and the
first expunge after a JS garbage collection failed with "TypeError:
d.bfq is not a function" (2000 Java objects with singleton classes and
idle gaps: 29 of 30 runs before, 0 of 30 after). JavaIntegrationPlugin
now connects every Weak/Soft/PhantomReference made with a queue to what
ReferenceQueue.poll()/remove() return. The same pattern is in
ObjectSpace, WeakIdentityHashMap, WeakValuedMap, ConcurrentWeakHashMap,
JarCache and WeakKeyValueIdentityMap.

android-src: Bundle is typed as Android's (getInt finds only an int,
another type gives the default and Android's W/Bundle warning in
logcat - JRuby passes a Ruby Integer to putExtra as a long), and has
the array/list methods (put/getStringArrayList, IntegerArrayList,
StringArray, IntArray, Bundle).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 android-src/android/os/Bundle.java            | 50 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../jrubyweb/teavm/JavaIntegrationPlugin.java | 31 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

